A good respiratory surface:

1. has a **large surface area** for the diffusion of gases (for example the many alveoli);
2. is **very thin** (one cell thick), so that the diffusion distance is short;
3. is **moist**, so that gases dissolve and diffuse in solution;
4. has a **rich blood supply** (dense network of capillaries) to carry gases away and keep the concentration gradient steep;
5. is **permeable** to oxygen and carbon dioxide;
6. is well **ventilated** to maintain a steep concentration gradient.

(Any four.)
